// Wave J7: a drive's lists show that drive's tracks, after any eject, pull
// or re-plug. The actual import (parseDeviceDB with Kaitai and SQLite) reads
// fake exports of two drives, GANDER1 (5 tracks) and IXIAN (7 tracks). The
// actual RekordboxFeature methods (activateChild, onTracksFound,
// onRekordboxDevicesFound, addDriveTracksRows, selectShownDriveTracks and,
// with the patch, resetTrackCache and dropRemovedList) and the actual
// constructor wiring between the devices and the tracks watchers run on
// stand-ins. The track cache runs the actual BaseTrackCache methods that
// fill and read it (buildIndex, updateIndexWithQuery, updateTracksInIndex,
// isCached, ensureCached, data) on a stand-in holding its members. The table
// stands in for RekordboxPlaylistModel: setPlaylist finds the playlist id by
// name, select() reads the playlist's track ids as BaseSqlTableModel::select
// does (building the cache index first, as filterAndSort does), and each cell
// is read as BaseSqlTableModel::data reads it (ensureCached when the id is not
// cached, then BaseTrackCache::data). LOAD reads the row's location
// (BaseExternalPlaylistModel::getTrack). tests/native/drive_track_cache_runner.py
// builds this; BASELINE is the source without mixxx-drive-track-cache.patch.
// EXPORT_MODE lists one playlist of a real export.pdb (fault 2).
